## Getting started

Download dependencies and build:

```bash
go mod tidy
make build
```

Run the CLI:

```bash
./{{ .Name }} hello --name World
# Hello, World!

./{{ .Name }} hello --name World --shout
# HELLO, WORLD!
```

Run tests:

```bash
make test
```

Install to `~/.local/bin`:

```bash
make install
```

Check version:

```bash
./{{ .Name }} --version
```

## Adding a new command

1. Create `cmd/<command_name>.go`:

```go
package cmd

import (
    "fmt"
    "github.com/spf13/cobra"
)

var myCmd = &cobra.Command{
    Use:   "mycommand",
    Short: "Do something",
    RunE: func(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {
        fmt.Println("Hello from mycommand")
        return nil
    },
}

func init() {
    rootCmd.AddCommand(myCmd)
}
```

2. That's it — `init()` wires it up automatically.

## Project structure

```
main.go                 Entry point; passes version to cmd.Execute
cmd/
├── root.go             Root cobra command and Execute() function
└── hello.go            Example subcommand with --name and --shout
internal/
└── logger/
    └── logger.go       Preconfigured slog JSON logger (opt-in)
```

## Enabling structured logging

Call `logger.Setup(false)` from `main()` to switch slog to JSON format on stderr:

```go
import "{{ .ModulePath }}/internal/logger"

func main() {
    logger.Setup(false)  // pass true for debug-level output
    cmd.Execute(Version)
}
```
